+# Evidence search prototype — 2026-11-14
+
+## Question and scope
+
+The November 13 capability inquiry identified reusable evidence discovery as a
+possible gap, while warning that an external platform or bespoke index could
+duplicate existing Free Software. This prototype tests the smallest operational
+alternative: a read-only command over the existing Git worktree, preferring
+installed `ripgrep` and falling back to `git grep`. It adds no service, index,
+database, boot hook, credentials, or source of truth. It is not enabled in
+production automation.
+
+## Existing-tool comparison
+
+- `ripgrep` 15.1.0 is already available in the current environment. The helper
+  uses its fixed-string, case-insensitive search over `records/` and
+  `government/`; it can see untracked working-tree files and omits binary data.
+- Git's built-in `git grep` is the fallback, with no new package dependency,
+  but searches tracked files only. This keeps the command usable in a minimal
+  checkout while making the fallback's coverage limitation explicit.
+- This is materially smaller than deploying Forgejo or Zulip: no service owner,
+  migration, new identity model, notification stream, or maintenance surface.
+  It also does not provide semantic search, cross-issue relationships, or an
+  expertise directory. If lexical retrieval is insufficient, this prototype
+  should not be mistaken for proof that a generated index or platform is
+  unnecessary.
+
+## Verification
+
+`tests/innovation-evidence-search-smoke.sh` uses a temporary Git repository and
+checks the ripgrep path when present, Git fallback, case-insensitive fixed
+string matching, no-match exit status, and empty-query handling. The implementation
+is POSIX `/bin/sh`, read-only, and requires only Git plus optional ripgrep.
+
+On this checkout, the helper returned 15 matching lines for the real query
+`handoff integrity` in about 0.019 seconds wall-clock (one local observation,
+not a comparative benchmark). Searching `canonical-checkout-integrity` returned
+the prior provenance report and related artifacts. This demonstrates retrieval
+of known material, not time saved versus a direct `rg` invocation or the rate of
+repeated investigation.
+
+The experiment verifies retrieval behavior, not a reduction in research time,
+re-derivation, or Founder attention. Those are outcome claims for an independent
+measurement window. No platform was installed and no operational dispatcher was
+modified. Keep or delete this prototype based on reviewer and outcome evidence.
+
+## Decision and remaining uncertainty
+
+The smallest useful trial appears to be a manual read-only search helper, not a
+generated global index. It has low adoption cost and is reversible. Its benefit
+is not yet demonstrated: direct `rg`/`git grep` commands already work, and a
+wrapper may be unnecessary ceremony. The next useful comparison is whether a
+researcher can retrieve a prior finding faster or more reliably using this
+helper than the existing direct command, measured on a real inquiry. If not,
+delete the helper rather than expanding it.
+
+This is a prototype only. No legislation, deployment, Judiciary measurement,
+or production integration is claimed.
